Fix v0.BitriseYMLConfigUpdateParams.location generation

The upstream spec wraps the enum ref in `allOf` (standard Swagger 2.0
idiom because JSON Schema draft-4 ignores siblings of a bare `$ref`).
go-swagger emits that as an embedded-struct wrapper, marshalling to
`{"location":{"WebsiteBitriseYMLLocation":"repository"}}` instead of
the plain string the API expects (known bug: go-swagger #436, #740).

Drop the `allOf` wrapper so the property uses a bare `$ref` and
go-swagger emits `Location WebsiteBitriseYMLLocation`.

--- a/swagger.json
+++ b/swagger.json
@@ -9918,12 +9918,7 @@
       "properties": {
         "location": {
           "description": "Location of bitrise.yml file. Enums(bitrise.io, repository)",
-          "allOf": [
-            {
-              "$ref": "#/definitions/website.BitriseYMLLocation"
-            }
-          ],
-          "example": "repository"
+          "$ref": "#/definitions/website.BitriseYMLLocation"
         }
       }
     },
